{
  "name": "413. BytePlus Seedance video: task object, strict seconds and size, task control fields, cancel only while queued (byteplus seedance task contract)",
  "description": "Pins TXE-6426 (contract C4, C5, C7, C9) for the byteplus provider on the unified video routes. Local fixture regression, no live provider calls: start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json and run with providerErrorFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. The fixture plays Ark's task API under /pp/byteplus: a query answers the task whose state its id names, and every query and DELETE is counted. Rows 2 to 7: a fractional seconds, a seconds outside 2 to 15, a size that names no Seedance tier and ratio exactly, a deadline outside Ark's range, client_reference_id and output_storage_uri are each refused with 400 caller_unsupported_parameter naming the field; before the change seconds was rounded, size was replaced by the nearest ratio and the two control fields were forwarded to Ark as unknown fields. Row 8 proves none of the six reached Ark. Rows 9 and 10: a create with the unified fields reaches Ark as ratio, resolution, a last_frame content item, callback_url and execution_expires_after. Rows 11 to 14: the task object carries provider_status, Ark's completion_tokens as usage.output_tokens, expires_at 24 hours after completion and a content_filter on a task Ark failed for its content; cancelled and expired are their own statuses (both read failed before). Rows 15 to 17: cancel on a queued task is one query and one DELETE and returns the task cancelled. Rows 18 to 20: cancel on a succeeded task is 400 provider_cancel_unsupported after one query and no DELETE, so the finished task's record is never removed.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "413.1 reset the fixture's counters and wire capture before the refused creates (byteplus seedance task contract)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": "{{providerErrorFixtureUrl}}/__reset"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the fixture reset its counters', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data[0].reset).to.eql(true);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
